The cleanup script is run daily from systemd on the backup server.

Installing:

1. copy the files to /etc/systemd/system
2. reload
      systemctl daemon reload
3. enable the timer, and start it
      systemctl enable /etc/systemd/system/cleanup*.timer
      systemctl start /etc/systemd/system/cleanup*.timer
4. confirm the timer is running
      systemctl list-timers | grep cleanup
5. run the service manually, and confirm success
      systemctl start cleanup_peregrine_backups.service
      systemctl status cleanup_peregrine_backups.service

